# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Methods
section("Methods"); add("## 3. Methods\n")
add(f"**Feature sets.** A: phase (two dummies, menses = reference). B: log1p estradiol and log1p progesterone. C: A + B. D: C + PSST + BDI + BAI. D2: D without PSST (added to test whether PSST overlaps with the DRSP outcome). Every set uses the same {n_rows('pooled')} complete rows.\n")
add(f"**Mathematical core (NumPy only).** Ridge loss L(w) = (1/n)||y - Xw||^2 + lambda||w||^2 on centred data (intercept unpenalised). (a) Normal equations (X'X + n lambda I)w = X'y and the SVD form w = V diag(s_i/(s_i^2 + n lambda)) U'y (pseudo-inverse at lambda = 0), checked against scikit-learn; (b) the same loss solved by gradient descent, mini-batch SGD, heavy-ball momentum and Adam; (c) gradient, Hessian H = (2/n)X'X + 2 lambda I, eigenvalues and condition number kappa = lambda_max/lambda_min, raw versus standardised; (d) ridge path, bias-variance by bootstrap over women, lambda by nested CV; (e) ridge as the MAP estimate under a Gaussian prior, with n lambda = sigma^2/tau^2. Notes in `docs/math/`.\n")
add(f"**Models and validation.** Baseline: the training-set mean. Ridge (own implementation, {calc('number of lambda values', len(cvlib.LAMS), '{:.0f}', 'src/cvlib.py', 'len(LAMS)')} values of lambda), random forest ({calc('number of RF leaf sizes', len(cvlib.RF_GRID), '{:.0f}', 'src/cvlib.py', 'len(RF_GRID)')} leaf sizes, {NTREE} trees), gradient boosting ({calc('number of GB settings', len(cvlib.GB_GRID), '{:.0f}', 'src/cvlib.py', 'len(GB_GRID)')} depth/trees settings, learning rate {LRB}). Outer loop: **leave-one-participant-out** (all sessions of a woman are held out together, so no woman is ever in both training and test); inner loop: {const('src/cvlib.py', r'k_inner=(\d+)', 'inner CV folds')}-fold cross-validation grouped by woman inside the training women for hyper-parameters (**nested CV**). Scaling and centring use training rows only. Random seed {calc('random seed', SEED, '{:.0f}', 'src/data.py', 'SEED')}. Additional transfer experiment: train on the cross-sectional women, test on the longitudinal women. Metrics: MAE, RMSE, R2 (pooled out-of-fold), and R2 versus the mean baseline (R2_oos = 1 - SSE_model/SSE_baseline). Uncertainty: percentile bootstrap resampling **women** (B = {const('src/phase4_report.py', r'\bB = (\d+)', 'bootstrap resamples B')}); paired differences use the same resampled women. Per-woman MAE/RMSE mean +/- SD are in `results/phase4_tables.md` (R2 has no per-woman value). Leakage checklist: `docs/leakage_checklist.md`.\n")
add("**Statistics.** Random-intercept mixed models (REML, statsmodels) on z-scored outcomes (as in the authors' R script), Wald tests, Holm adjustment over the three phase contrasts; permutation tests that keep the design (phase labels shuffled within woman, estradiol shuffled within woman for the within test, woman-mean estradiol shuffled across women for the between test). Estradiol split into a within-woman part (value minus the woman's own mean) and a between-woman part (her mean). Multiple comparisons: Holm and Benjamini-Hochberg FDR over the paired hormone comparisons. **Credibility checks:** a negative control (emotion-recognition accuracy and speed from the same inputs) and a sanity check (cycle phase from hormones, balanced accuracy and confusion matrix).\n")
