add(f"\n(Sample sizes: pooled {nn('pooled')}; longitudinal {nn('long')}. 'not reached' = not converged within the iteration cap.) Standardising brings kappa to a few units, so GD converges in a few dozen steps; on unscaled data it is hopelessly slow. **Tuned heavy-ball momentum** (beta = ((sqrt(kappa)-1)/(sqrt(kappa)+1))^2, lr = 4/(sqrt(L)+sqrt(mu))^2) reaches the same accuracy in {val(P3BM, dict(sample='pooled', problem='raw (raw hormones, unscaled)'), 'hb_iters', '{:,.0f}', label='tuned momentum iterations, raw, pooled')} iterations on the raw problem (kappa {val(P3BM, dict(sample='pooled', problem='raw (raw hormones, unscaled)'), 'kappa', '{:,.0f}', label='kappa raw pooled')}) where GD did not converge, and {val(P3BM, dict(sample='pooled', problem='log1p hormones, unscaled'), 'hb_iters', '{:,.0f}', label='tuned momentum iterations, log1p, pooled')} versus {val(P3BM, dict(sample='pooled', problem='log1p hormones, unscaled'), 'gd_iters', '{:,.0f}', label='GD iterations, log1p, pooled')} for GD on the log1p problem: about sqrt(kappa) steps instead of kappa. "
    f"GD with learning rate 2.1 / lambda_max {val(P3B, dict(sample='pooled', optimizer='GD', lr_mult=2.1), 'final_rel_subopt', '{:.1e}', label='GD at 2.1/lmax')}, as theory (stability needs lr < 2/lambda_max) predicts, while 1.9 / lambda_max converged (relative suboptimality {val(P3B, dict(sample='pooled', optimizer='GD', lr_mult=1.9), 'final_rel_subopt', '{:.1e}', label='GD at 1.9/lmax')}). SGD with a constant step stalls at a noise floor that grows with the step ({val(P3B, dict(sample='pooled', optimizer='SGD', lr_mult=0.01), 'final_rel_subopt', '{:.1e}', label='SGD lr 0.01/lmax')} at 0.01/lambda_max versus {val(P3B, dict(sample='pooled', optimizer='SGD', lr_mult=1.0), 'final_rel_subopt', '{:.1e}', label='SGD lr 1/lmax')} at 1/lambda_max). Figures: `results/fig_3b_*.png`, `fig_3c_hessian.png`.\n")
